    "title": "Jordan Spieth in elite company because of majors, not style points",
    "text": "SPORTSJordan Spieth in elite company because of majors, not style pointsAssociated PressJuly 24, 2017, 10:27 a.m. ETSOUTHPORT, England - Jordan Spieth was happy enough to see his name on the claret jug without wondering where he fit in among the rest of the British Open champions whose names are engraved on the oldest trophy in golf.In that respect, nothing has changed.Spieth wasn't keen on comparisons when he became the youngest Masters champion since Tiger Woods, the youngest U.S. Open champion since Bobby Jones or the youngest to win two majors since Gene Sarazen. And now that Jack Nicklaus is part of the conversation, he shies away from them even more.",
